{#- Practice quiz of every game, from @hostelgames/core. Include it where the quiz belongs
    ({% include "quiz.njk" %}, usually rules page and quick start). Hidden without JavaScript.
    It loads the game's own /assets/quiz.js (the rules), which starts the core engine
    /assets/core/quiz.js. Tests: siteTests({ …, quiz: ["rules", "quickstart"] }).

    Texts (i18n): qH heading (on the quick start quick.tryH, if the game has it), qLead, qQ
    (question), qNext (button to the next question), quiz.* (the game's explanations);
    qYes, qNo and quiz.right / wrong / yes / no / score are standard texts of the core.

    The picture of the question comes from quiz-stage.njk: core default two cards ("on top"
    qTop in #topCard, "your card" qMine in #myCard). A game with another picture (dice …)
    puts its own quiz-stage.njk into its _includes. -#}
{%- set t = lang.t -%}
{%- set quizH = t.qH -%}
{%- if subpath == "quickstart/" and t.quick and t.quick.tryH %}{% set quizH = t.quick.tryH %}{% endif -%}
<section id="practice" class="js-only">
  <h2>{{ quizH }}</h2>
  <p class="lead">{{ t.qLead | safe }}</p>
  <div class="trainer" aria-live="polite">
    {% include "quiz-stage.njk" %}
    <p class="q">{{ t.qQ }}</p>
    <div class="btns" id="btns">
      <button class="yes" data-a="1">{{ t.qYes }}</button>
      <button class="no" data-a="0">{{ t.qNo }}</button>
    </div>
    <div class="fb" id="fb"></div>
    <button class="next" id="next" hidden>{{ t.qNext }}</button>
    <div class="score" id="score"></div>
  </div>
  <script type="application/json" id="quiz-text">{{ t.quiz | dump | safe }}</script>
  <script type="module" src="/assets/quiz.js?v={{ assetVersion }}"></script>
</section>
